Q: How can I iterate over an enum? A: <p>C++26 is expected to have the first version of Reflection features.  This means we can iterate over the <code>std::meta::info</code> objects representing the enumerators of type <code>E</code> like this:</p>
<pre><code>template for (auto constexpr e: std::define_static_array(enumerators_of(^^E)))
</code></pre>
<p>Within the loop, we can access the values using the splice operator <code>[:e:]</code>.</p>
<p>Full demo:</p>
<pre><code>#include &lt;meta&gt;
#include &lt;print&gt;
#include &lt;string_view&gt;

enum class nation {
    england,
    ireland,
    scotland,
    wales
};

std::string_view to_sv(nation n)
{
    switch (n) {
    case nation::england: return &quot;England&quot;;
    case nation::ireland: return &quot;Ireland&quot;;
    case nation::scotland: return &quot;Scotland&quot;;
    case nation::wales: return &quot;Wales&quot;;
    }
    return &quot;abroad&quot;;
}

int main()
{
    template for (auto constexpr e: define_static_array(enumerators_of(^^nation))) {
        std::println(&quot;{}&quot;, to_sv([:e:]));
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>If you don't yet have access to a suitable compiler, then you can <a href="https://godbolt.org/z/b8K7aGM8h" rel="nofollow noreferrer">preview this on Compiler Explorer</a>.</p>

Q: Get namespace of current page in MediaWiki userscript A: <p>You get the current namespace number in JavaScript like this:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>ns = mw.config.get ('wgNamespaceNumber');
</code></pre>

Q: Concept that requires both a const and non-const overload to be present A: <p>Icharchurski answer can be generalized to template function through allowing to test for given instances:</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>template &lt;typename T, typename out,typename ...in&gt;
concept HasNonConstFoo =
    requires { static_cast&lt;out (T::*)(in...)&gt;(&amp;T::member_function); };

template &lt;typename T, typename out,typename ...in&gt;
concept HasConstFoo =
    requires { static_cast&lt;out (T::*)(in...) const&gt;(&amp;T::member_function); };

template &lt;typename T, typename out,typename ...in&gt;
concept Both = HasNonConstFoo&lt;T,out,in...&gt; &amp;&amp; HasConstFoo&lt;T,out,in...&gt;;
</code></pre>
